MDL101, K15, F1: the same byte order mark in a file without [client], the
connection coming from the command line. GLib rejects the file, so mydumper
ignores all of it and dumps users.email in plaintext, exit 0. The MySQL client
library still reads the file as its defaults file (F12) and rejects it too
("Found option without preceding group"); this scenario shows whether the
connection survives that when host, user and password are explicit.
-- scenario --
tool: mydumper
versions: >= v0.19.1-1
args: --defaults-file /work/defaults.cnf --host mysql --user e2e --password e2e-password --database app
lint: MDL101, MDL112
when < v0.19.3-1
# No pre-processor before v0.19.3-1, hence no bracket state leak (MDL112).
lint: MDL101
end
expect config-loaded: false
expect exit: 0
expect connected: true
expect column app.users.email: plaintext
-- defaults.cnf.esc --
\xef\xbb\xbf[mydumper]\nthreads=2\n\n[`app`.`users`]\n`email`=random_string\n
